Hi,

Thank you very much for your advice! I have been exploring my data following your indications. Here is what I have:

Sample size for the three datasets are: 51, 51 and 32 skulls. I do not think that they are too small. In fact, the third one (32) does not seem to be more biased than the other ones (51) as you can see below.

I have not found any outlayer. I have performed several PCAs and I have explored until the 6th PC.

All the CR values are significant with a P value of 0.001, so the modular hypothesis tested provides the lowest value of all permutations.

I have estimated the bias as suggested for each dataset:
CR1 = 0.6136, bias1 = 0.09617
CR2 = 0.6668, bias2 = 0.084847
CR3 = 0.7256, bias3 = 0.084541

Maybe, the best option is to show the observed CR values together with the corrected CR values (CR + bias equals the average of the bootstrapp distribution) with a caution note about this bias.

What do you think?

Thank you very much again for your help!!!

Best,

AL

