Hi all,

As far as I am aware, if 2 structures are highly modular (as revealed from modularity.test) then I would expect results from integration.test to be non-significant. However, I find highly significant results for both a modularity hypothesis, as well as an integration hypothesis using the same sets of landmarks.

Am I making a mistake somewhere here? Or perhaps this is due to my lack of understanding...

land.gps2 <- c('a', 'a', 'a', 'b',  'b', 'a', 'a', 'a',  'a', 'a', 'a',  'b', 'b',  'b',  'b', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a',
               'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a', 'a',
               'a', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b', 'b')
modTest1 <- modularity.test(Hfemale.gdf.symm$shape, land.gps2, CI = T, iter = 999)

#CR: 0.8748
#P-value: 0.001

IT <- integration.test(Hfemale.gdf.symm$shape, partition.gp <http://partition.gp>=land.gps2, iter=999)

#r-PLS: 0.941
#P-value: 0.006

Thanks,
Sam

